there to learn?

00:12:54.222 --> 00:12:57.241
Can you tell us a little
bit about that mix?

00:13:00.139 --> 00:13:05.627
&gt;&gt; I think Startup Garage is very friendly
to everyone across that spectrum and

00:13:05.627 --> 00:13:08.639
frankly people change pathway through.

00:13:08.639 --> 00:13:13.801
So I would say one of my classmates,
I think he could have been 50 50,

00:13:13.801 --> 00:13:18.895
and then he just decided ultimately
he didn't have one specific idea.

00:13:18.895 --> 00:13:20.011
It didn't feel the right time in his
life to start something but he's still,

00:13:20.011 --> 00:13:20.937
I think has in the back of his
head that he'll do it eventually.

00:13:20.937 --> 00:13:26.471
So I think Startup Garage in

00:13:26.471 --> 00:13:34.417
particular is very welcoming to that.

00:13:34.417 --> 00:13:39.029
There are other resources, other
similar classes to Startup Garage and

00:13:39.029 --> 00:13:44.247
the D school and in the engineering school
that are called either Lean Launchpad or

00:13:44.247 --> 00:13:48.348
Launchpad, they're confusingly
named very similar things.

00:13:48.348 --> 00:13:52.253
But those are a bit more intense
if you will, and I think for

00:13:52.253 --> 00:13:54.499
folks who are very focused on it.

00:13:54.499 --> 00:13:57.873
But I would say Startup Garage
is very friendly

00:13:57.873 --> 00:14:01.345
to any front light interest
to heavy interest.

00:14:01.345 --> 00:14:03.888
&gt;&gt; Yeah,
I would very much agree with that.

00:14:03.888 --> 00:14:08.677
I think that it's like anything else
in the world that's kind of like you

00:14:08.677 --> 00:14:12.064
get out of it what you put
into it type of situation.

00:14:12.064 --> 00:14:16.200
And I think a lot of people go
into the process looking for

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.376
